12 MX | solution-layout.md:101-103: repository formatting configuration plus an instruction-design preference.
  - XP m=D c=M rel=RUN-009 | Deterministic repository-wide formatting and code-style configuration lives in the root .editorconfig.
    s: Formatting conventions kept only in a contributor document without .editorconfig rules: allowed by RUN-009 ('follow .editorconfig' when present); M places them in .editorconfig.
  - IA m=D | Prefer enforceable tooling configuration over restating mechanical formatting rules in instructions (instruction-system design).
13 XP m=D c=M rel=SEC-001,WF-004 | Ignore generated and local artifacts (bin, obj, .vs, node_modules, dist, .angular, TestResults, coverage, local secret/config overrides) (repository hygiene not in the oracle).
  e: where applicable
  s: A repository whose .gitignore lacks TestResults and coverage outputs: allowed by the oracle; M's default ignores them.
14 CO DEP-026~ m=MN c=M | Do not ignore files that are part of the Development configuration contract such as a non-secret appsettings.Development.json (DEP-026 requires it to provide the usable local configuration).
15 CO DEP-018 GOV-013~ ARC-020~ m=MN | Docker, deployment manifests, Kubernetes, cloud/messaging infrastructure and extra services only for a concrete requirement.
16 CO WF-020 | Evidence-based static security review, not a penetration test (WF-020).
17 XW m=M c=M rel=WF-009,WF-020 | The scan report states the limitations of static review (runtime, infrastructure, business-logic, authorization-bypass, deployment, dynamic exploitation).
  s: A scan report listing findings without a limitations statement: consistent with WF-020/WF-009; M requires the statement.
18 XW m=M c=M rel=WF-020,WF-009 | Security scan report shape: Scope, Limitations, severity Summary table, Findings and Layer Results for the seven layers with PASS / FINDINGS / NOT APPLICABLE / NOT CHECKED.
  s: A free-form scan report with confirmed findings and verification items: consistent with WF-020; M's report shape is not followed.
19 CO WF-001~ c=M | Read .claude/rules/security.md before scanning (apply the applicable rules).
20 CO WF-020 | Concrete risks, context, confirmed vs needs-verification, contextual severity not raw CVSS (WF-020).
21 CO GOV-013~ WF-020~ m=MN | Do not require security mechanisms the project does not need.
22 CO WF-001~ c=M | Use the project's security-related guidance during the scan (apply applicable rules/skills).
23 CO WF-021 m=M | Scan works without any specific external tool; tooling is evidence only (WF-021).
24 CO WF-021 WF-020~ m=MN | A scanner-reported issue is reported only after inspecting the code and reachability.
25 XW m=D c=M rel=WF-020 | OWASP Top 10:2025 as an awareness taxonomy when it genuinely fits, without forced mappings.
  s: A scan report without OWASP categorisation: consistent with the oracle; M's default maps findings where it fits.
26 CO WF-007 WF-009~ | Determine existing surfaces; skip irrelevant checks instead of reporting failures (risk-scoped checks, truthful reporting).
27 CO WF-007 | All applicable layers for full audits; affected layers first for targeted changes (WF-007).
28 CO WF-021 WF-020 | Use available tooling; inspect, determine reachability and report with appropriate confidence.
29 CO WF-020 | Severity from exploitability, exposure, privileges, data, blast radius, reliability, compensating controls (WF-020).
30 XW m=M c=M rel=WF-020 | Five-level scan severity scale (Critical used sparingly ... Info) with its definitions; WF-020 requires contextual severity but no scale.
  s: Findings rated High/Low only with contextual justification: consistent with WF-020; M's scale is not used.
31 CO WF-020 SEC-001~ SEC-010~ SEC-005~ SEC-009~ m=MN | Not automatically safe: Development secrets, Debug-level sensitive logging, route guards, hidden buttons, CORS instead of authorization.
32 MX | security-scan SKILL.md:151-161: finding fields and report shape, plus an ownership rule for the skill text.
  - XW m=M c=M rel=WF-020,WF-009 | Every confirmed finding includes severity, location, title, evidence, risk, impact, smallest remediation and OWASP category when applicable, in the prescribed report shape.
    s: Findings reported with evidence and severity but without remediation or OWASP category: consistent with WF-020; M's fields are missing.
  - IA m=MN | Do not duplicate the implementation guidance of the referenced skills inside the scan (instruction ownership).
33 CO WF-020 c=M | Uncertain findings labelled NEEDS VERIFICATION (WF-020 distinguishes confirmed from needs-verification; the label is the means).
34 CO WF-009 c=M | Layer status PASS/FINDINGS/NOT APPLICABLE/NOT CHECKED; never mark an uninspected layer as passed (WF-009 equivalent statuses).
35 CO GOV-012 SEC-008~ SEC-006~ GOV-013~ SEC-016~ m=MN | Smallest secure change; no unnecessary auth systems, custom crypto, blanket encryption, redundant [Authorize], libraries to satisfy the scan, or disabling functionality.
36 CO WF-020 WF-009 | Scan completion criteria (inspected layers, evidence, labels, contextual severity, limitations, no unchecked PASS).
37 CO WF-020 | Concrete risks; confirmed vs needs verification (WF-020).
38 CO WF-020~ WF-012~ c=M | Avoid known false positives (evidence-based findings, no manufactured findings).
39 CO WF-020 | Investigation prompts are used to find evidence, not as automatic vulnerability declarations (WF-020).
40 CO WF-020~ WF-009~ m=MN c=M | Do not claim a static scan proves design security.
41 XW m=D c=M rel=WF-020,DEP-004 | Supply-chain layer checklist (direct/transitive vulnerabilities, advisories, actual usage, patched versions, untrusted NuGet sources, npm audit by category, lockfile review) (EXC-015 investigative prompts; read as a DEFAULT scan checklist).
  t: when the layer applies
  s: A security scan that skips untrusted package-source review: consistent with WF-020; M's checklist includes it.
42 CO WF-020 m=MN | Advisory CVSS not converted directly into application severity (WF-020).
43 CO GOV-014 m=MN | Do not upgrade packages during a scan unless asked (GOV-014 scope).
  e: when asked
44 XW m=D c=M rel=WF-020,SEC-001 | Secrets/configuration layer checklist (file types to search; production debug flags, certificate-validation bypass, credential-bearing URLs, verbose production errors, committed .env) (EXC-015 investigative prompts).
  s: A scan that searches only .json files for secrets: consistent with WF-020; M's checklist covers the listed file types.
45 CO WF-020 WF-012~ SEC-006~ SEC-009~ m=MN c=M | Not automatically reported: fallback-protected endpoints, intended bare [Authorize], AllowAnyOrigin for public non-credentialed APIs, MD5/SHA1 checksums, platform-encrypted data, obvious fake credentials, secure defaults (contextual findings).
46 CO SEC-001 m=MN d=WF | A real secret is not suppressed because it appears in a Development file (SEC-001 applies to all committed files).
47 XW m=D c=M rel=WF-020,SEC-003,SEC-004 | Injection layer checklist (SQL from untrusted input, command execution, path traversal, SSRF, Angular sanitizer bypass/DOM, unsafe deserialization) (EXC-015 investigative prompts).
  s: A scan that does not check SSRF via user-controlled URLs: consistent with WF-020; M's checklist includes it.
48 XP m=D c=M rel=SEC-003 | When command execution is genuinely needed, prefer APIs separating executable and arguments and validate/constrain external input (technique beyond SEC-003's validation).
  s: Process.Start with a single command string built from validated input: satisfies SEC-003; M prefers argument-list APIs.
49 CO SEC-003~ m=M c=M | Normalize user-influenced paths (incl. archive extraction) and verify they remain within the storage boundary: validation of untrusted input where assumptions matter (SEC-003).
50 CO SEC-003~ m=MN c=M | Do not deserialize untrusted payloads into arbitrary runtime types (BinaryFormatter, unsafe TypeNameHandling): untrusted data handling (SEC-003).
51 CO SEC-016 | Passwords with established one-way hashing facilities, not reversible encryption (SEC-016).
52 CO SEC-008 SEC-016~ SEC-001~ d=WF | Flag security-sensitive MD5/SHA1/ECB, hardcoded keys, custom password hashing, home-grown encryption (SEC-008, SEC-016).
53 CO SEC-006 SEC-005~ | Evaluate effective authorization incl. global/fallback policies (SEC-006).
54 CO SEC-006 WF-020~ | Confirm [AllowAnonymous]/public surfaces are intentional; do not report every public endpoint.
55 XW m=D c=M rel=WF-020,SEC-005,SEC-016,SEC-018 | Access-control layer checklist (identifier-only access/IDOR; local-account hashing, reset, lockout, enumeration, credential storage) (EXC-015 investigative prompts).
  s: A scan that reviews authorization attributes but not identifier-only access paths: consistent with WF-020; M's checklist includes IDOR.
56 CO SEC-005 | Verify ownership/tenant/permission/resource policy where required; client-side filtering is not authorization (SEC-005).
57 CO SEC-017 WF-020~ c=M | Bearer/OIDC validation check without requiring every TokenValidationParameters setting or a universal ClockSkew; flag intentionally weakened validation (SEC-017).
58 XW m=D c=M rel=SEC-016,SEC-018 | Local-account review checklist (hashing, reset, lockout, enumeration) during scans (EXC-015 investigative prompts).
  s: A scan of an app with local accounts that does not look at lockout: consistent with WF-020; M's checklist includes it.
59 CO SEC-009 SEC-005~ c=M | CORS is not authorization; origins checked against the browser-client model; AllowAnyOrigin valid for public non-credentialed APIs (SEC-009).
60 CO SEC-011 | CSRF review when browser credentials are sent automatically; Angular provides no server-side CSRF protection (SEC-011).
